index fa71dc0..60955c1 100644
--- a/DOCS/man/options.rst
+++ b/DOCS/man/options.rst
@@ -6926,6 +6926,21 @@ them.
     :system:   No manual syncing, depend on the layer mechanic and the next drawable
     :feedback: Same as precise but uses the presentation feedback core mechanism
 
+``--macos-parent-layer=<pointer>``
+    Show the video in a layer inside another layer, filling it, instead of
+    in a window of mpv's own (macOS and Vulkan (macvk) only). The value is a
+    ``CALayer *`` of the same process, cast to ``intptr_t``, which makes this
+    only useful through libmpv. mpv adds its Metal layer to it as a sublayer
+    that follows its size, and makes no window or view, so it takes no
+    input. The layer has to be in a window when a video output opens. The
+    application's main thread has to run its run loop while one opens and
+    closes, which rules out ending mpv from that thread while one is open.
+
+    Unlike with the render API, the video keeps its own layer, so everything
+    that depends on one works as in mpv's own window: Vulkan, HDR, and
+    presentation timing. To show it under an application's content, give it
+    a layer below that content's.
+
 ``--macos-menu-shortcuts=<yes|no>``
     Enables the default menu bar shortcuts (default: yes). The menu bar shortcuts always take
     precedence over any other shortcuts, they are not propagated to the mpv core and they can't be
